{
  "_doc": "src/shared/minimap.ts (tool 1, top-down map). World = local NED of the frame: north n, east e, metres from the EKF origin; yaw = rad clockwise from north (yawFromQuat, quaternion [w, x, y, z] body FRD to world NED). Trail: pushTrail(trail, p, seg, minStep, max) with p = NED position (only p[0] north and p[1] east count): it appends [n, e] when the distance to the last point is >= minStep (0.5 m, equality adds), empties the trail and starts again with the new point when seg differs from the trail seg (the first push of an empty trail has no seg to compare), and drops the oldest points above max (1200). A new hello = emptyTrail() (the web does it, not this function). fitView(points, fence, sizePx, marginPx): centre = middle of the bounding box of the points and of the fence square; scale = (distance from the centre to the farthest point, or to the fence centre + radius) / max(1, sizePx / 2 - marginPx), never below 0.05 m/px; nothing to show = origin at 0.05. followView = vehicle at the centre, scale = max(fitScale, 0.25). scaleBar(scale, maxPx) = the largest m x 10^k, m in {1, 2, 5}, with metres / scale <= maxPx (relative slack 1e-12), px = metres / scale. toScreen returns px from the CENTRE of the view, y down: north up x = (e - centerE) / scale, y = -(n - centerN) / scale; heading up (yaw rad): x = (-dn sin(yaw) + de cos(yaw)) / scale, y = -(dn cos(yaw) + de sin(yaw)) / scale. viewAngles = rad clockwise from the top of the screen where the vehicle arrow and the north mark point (north up: arrow = yaw, north = 0; heading up: arrow = 0, north = -yaw). The desktop port compares numbers with the tolerance below; scaleLabel strings are exact.",
